  "slug": "artist:49ers",
  "name": "49ers",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in 1988 in Brescia, Italy, by producer Gianfranco Bortolotti, the 49ers project became a significant force in the international Italo house scene. The group, named after the American football team, achieved major chart success in 1990 with the singles \"Touch Me\" and \"Don't You Love Me,\" both of which reached number-one on the Billboard Hot Dance Club Play chart. Their debut single, \"Die Walküre,\" utilized a vocal sample from Freeez's \"I.O.U.\" while \"Touch Me\" incorporated a sample from Aretha Franklin's \"Rock-a-Lott.\" The group's vocal identity was complex, with models and singers like Dawn Mitchell and Alysha Warren fronting the act, often lip-syncing or providing uncredited studio performances. By 1992, they released their second album, \"Playing with My Heart,\" before eventually disbanding in 1998, though they later returned for a 2010 single featuring samples from Charlie Chaplin's 1936 film \"Modern Times.\"",
